  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "But I determined this with myself, that I would not come again to you in heaviness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "For if I make you sorry, who is he then that maketh me glad, but the same which is made sorry by me?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "And I wrote this same unto you, lest, when I came, I should have sorrow from them of whom I ought to rejoice; having confidence in you all, that my joy is the joy of you all.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "For out of much affliction and anguish of heart I wrote unto you with many tears; not that ye should be grieved, but that ye might know the love which I have more abundantly unto you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "But if any have caused grief, he hath not grieved me, but in part: that I may not overcharge you all.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Sufficient to such a man is this punishment, which was inflicted of many.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "So that contrariwise ye ought rather to forgive him, and comfort him, lest perhaps such a one should be swallowed up with overmuch sorrow.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Wherefore I beseech you that ye would confirm your love toward him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "For to this end also did I write, that I might know the proof of you, whether ye be obedient in all things.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "To whom ye forgive any thing, I forgive also: for if I forgave any thing, to whom I forgave it, for your sakes forgave I it in the person of Christ;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Lest Satan should get an advantage of us: for we are not ignorant of his devices.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Furthermore, when I came to Troas to preach Christ’s gospel, and a door was opened unto me of the Lord,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "I had no rest in my spirit, because I found not Titus my brother: but taking my leave of them, I went from thence into Macedonia.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Now thanks be unto God, which always causeth us to triumph in Christ, and maketh manifest the savour of his knowledge by us in every place.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "For we are unto God a sweet savour of Christ, in them that are saved, and in them that perish:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "To the one we are the savour of death unto death; and to the other the savour of life unto life. And who is sufficient for these things?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "For we are not as many, which corrupt the word of God: but as of sincerity, but as of God, in the sight of God speak we in Christ.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 2:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:2:17"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
